<title>JAPAN: Toyota shares fall after news of output suspension.</title>
<headline>Toyota shares fall after news of output suspension.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Toyota Motor Corp shares fell in Monday afternoon trade, depressed by profit-taking after news that it would suspend domestic production for a day after a fire destroyed a factory owned by one of its component suppliers, brokers said.</p>
<p>As of 0446 GMT, the shares were down 30 yen at 3,100 yen.  </p>
<p>An Aisin Seiki Co Ltd spokesman said on Monday that a fire over the weekend completely destroyed one of its plants supplying vehicle parts to Toyota.</p>
<p>About 90 percent of the company's products are shipped to Toyota, the spokesman said.</p>
<p>Aisin Seiki shares were down 110 yen at 1,660.</p>
</text>
